{
  "id": "inlay_hints/parameter_hints/03_suppression",
  "topic": "inlay_hints",
  "subtopic": "parameter_hints",
  "title": "Hint suppression",
  "summary": "Named arguments and `/*name=*/` comments suppress parameter hints",
  "prose": "An argument spelled like its parameter, or a bare member of that name, needs no hint; a qualified name or a member reached through an object is no match. A comment naming another parameter suppresses nothing.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#1877"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "void draw(int width, int height);\n\nvoid use() {\n    int width = 5;\n    int h = 2;\n    draw(width, h);\n    draw(/*width=*/1, /*height=*/2);\n    draw(/*margin=*/6, 7);\n}\n\nstruct Sizes {\n    static int width;\n    int height;\n\n    void member() {\n        draw(5, height);\n    }\n};\n\nvoid qualified(Sizes s) {\n    draw(Sizes::width, 3);\n    draw(4, s.height);\n}\n",
      "markers": []
